.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-enforce 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-enforce \- Run every configured rule, including kinds that execute a configured command
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten enforce\fR [\fB\-\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-half\fR] [\fB\-\-keyed\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-inputs\-digest\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run every configured rule, including kinds that execute a configured command
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR \fI<rule>\fR
Run only the declared rules with these ids (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-half\fR
Judge only the tree half (receipt\-keyed on the index) or the live half of the rows
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
tree: Rows whose verdict is a function of the indexed tree alone
.IP \(bu 2
live: Every other row, and any row whose half cannot be established
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-keyed\-base\fR \fI<keyed_base>\fR
A ref whose merge base the tree half\*(Aqs receipt keys, admitting ratchets against it (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-inputs\-digest\fR
With \-\-half tree: print a digest of the out\-of\-tree state that half reads, and judge nothing
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
